# Notebook outputs are stripped on the way into git by the "nbstripout" filter.
#
# These lines say *which* files the filter applies to and are committed, so every
# clone inherits them.  The filter *driver* — the command git actually runs — is
# per-clone state in .git/config and is NOT committed: run
#
#     bash setup_nbstripout.sh
#
# once after cloning.  Without that step git warns about an undefined filter and
# notebooks are committed with their outputs intact.
#
# That script also configures which metadata keys are stripped (kernel choice,
# Python patch version) — so run it rather than a bare "nbstripout --install",
# which would strip less and leave notebooks churning between contributors.
*.ipynb filter=nbstripout
*.ipynb diff=ipynb
